name: Recover an unfinished context copy after an owned process crash, with exact cursor and explicit discard
size: 120x36
cwd: @TMP_TARGET
env-unset: ANTHROPIC_API_KEY OPENAI_API_KEY KUZUSHI_MODEL KUZUSHI_LANGGRAPH_BRIDGE NODE_OPTIONS NO_COLOR
env: HOME=@TMP_HOME KUZUSHI_SKIP_ONBOARDING=1 KUZUSHI_REDUCED_MOTION=1
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/context_checkpoint.py @TMP_TARGET @ART @TMP_HOME seed
require-wrapper-flow:
launch: --target @TMP_TARGET
require-live-snap: 30 KUZUSHI | ready
submit: setg ui.auto_open_activity false
submit: setg ui.auto_open_viz false
submit: logs
submit: run context:build {"enrichment":false}
require-live-snap: 35 Build project context: | inventory
submit: use threat-model
submit: options threat-model:import
submit: set path .kuzushi/manual-context.json
submit: set activate false
submit: set label Recovery source context
submit: run threat-model:import
require-live-snap: 35 threat-model:import saved | imported
submit: map
require-live-snap: 25 SYSTEM SUMMARY | mapped
nav-mode:
keys: u
require-live-snap: 25 Map ✓ | accepted-base
submit: scan batch
require-live-snap: 25 PLAN A STUDY | study
keys: Down Down Down Enter Enter
require-live-snap: 25 CONTEXT SUMMARY | inspected
keys: e
require-live-snap: 20 EDIT CONTEXT COPY | editor
keys: Enter C-u
paste-file: @ART/checkpoint-text.txt
keys: C-Home Right Right
require-live-snap: 25 Draft saved locally | checkpointed
ask: Does the editor show local checkpoint status separately from context acceptance and spending, while preserving multiline text and the cursor?
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/context_checkpoint.py @TMP_TARGET @ART @TMP_HOME crash
require-exit: 10
env: HOME=@TMP_HOME KUZUSHI_SKIP_ONBOARDING=1 KUZUSHI_REDUCED_MOTION=1 NO_COLOR=1
launch: --target @TMP_TARGET
require-live-snap: 30 KUZUSHI | restarted
submit: scan batch
require-live-snap: 25 PLAN A STUDY | restarted-study
keys: Down Down Down Enter Enter
require-live-snap: 25 CONTEXT SUMMARY | reinspected
keys: e
require-live-snap: 25 1 saved draft | recovery-choice
expect: exact context
resize: 160x48
live-snap: recovery-160x48
resize: 96x89
live-snap: recovery-96x89
resize: 80x24
live-snap: recovery-80x24
resize: 60x20
live-snap: recovery-60x20
resize: 40x12
require-live-snap: 20 RECOVER CONTEXT DRAFT | recovery-40x12
expect: Enter recover
expect: ▸
ask: Is the saved draft distinguishable and recoverable with visible controls across all six sizes, without silently choosing a draft or approving work?
resize: 120x36
keys: Enter
require-live-snap: 25 Checkpoint α | recovered
expect: second line 東京
keys: Delete
require-live-snap: 25 Chckpoint α | cursor-preserved
require-live-snap: 25 Draft saved locally | edited-checkpoint
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/context_checkpoint.py @TMP_TARGET @ART @TMP_HOME edited
keys: Escape
require-live-snap: 20 ↑↓ Enter edit | edit-fields
keys: d
require-live-snap: 20 DISCARD CONTEXT DRAFT | discard-review
keys: Enter
require-live-snap: 25 CONTEXT SUMMARY | discarded
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/context_checkpoint.py @TMP_TARGET @ART @TMP_HOME resolved
keys: e
require-live-snap: 20 EDIT CONTEXT COPY | no-resurrection
expect-not: Chckpoint α
expect-not: RECOVER CONTEXT DRAFT
ask: Does recovery retain exact text and cursor, while explicit discard prevents resurrection and preserves the source context, global selection, observations and spending?
keys: C-c
require-exit: 10
